 object. The vector style","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"layer defines the appearance of any content supplied by the shape source. You","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"can update a shape source by setting its ","type":"text"},{"code":"shape","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" or ","type":"text"},{"code":"URL","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" property.","type":"text"}]},"doc://org.swift.MyProject/documentation/MapLibre-Native-for-iOS/GeoJSON":{"title":"Working with GeoJSON Data","kind":"article","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/maplibre-native-for-ios\/geojson","abstract":[],"identifier":"doc:\/\/org.swift.MyProject\/documentation\/MapLibre-Native-for-iOS\/GeoJSON","role":"article"},"doc://org.swift.MyProject/documentation/MapLibre/MLNFeature":{"title":"MLNFeature","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/maplibre\/mlnfeature","abstract":[{"text":"The ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/org.swift.MyProject\/documentation\/MapLibre\/MLNFeature","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":"  protocol is used to provide details about geographic features","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"contained in an ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/org.swift.MyProject\/documentation\/MapLibre\/MLNShapeSource","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" or ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/org.swift.MyProject\/documentation\/MapLibre\/MLNVectorTileSource","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" object. Each concrete","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"subclass of ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/org.swift.MyProject\/documentation\/MapLibre\/MLNShape","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" in turn has a subclass that conforms to this protocol. A","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"feature object associates a shape with an optional identifier and attributes.","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MLNFeature"}],"identifier":"doc: